  "findings": [
    "target/xtensa/helper.c is byte-identical in the identified native compile source and frozen browser source: TLB fill, unaligned and transaction failure paths have the same C text.",
    "hw/misc/esp32s3_cache.c differs only by browser cache-stack diagnostics and calls around MMU/block reads; the actual cache/MMU state-operation text is preserved. Diagnostics can affect timing, so this is not native/WASM runtime equivalence.",
    "target/xtensa/exc_helper.c differs by the browser cpu-timers include and high-priority IRQ-entry note. Exception, cause/vaddr, debug, waiti, relocated-vector, handle_interrupt and cpu_exec_interrupt function bodies are unchanged.",
    "target/xtensa/op_helper.c adds browser high_priority_irq_return and high_priority_irq_yield helpers plus cpu-timers include. Existing native helper bodies are unchanged.",
    "accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c current native/browser text differs only by browser C-stack restore around cpu_exec_setjmp. cpu_exec_step_atomic text is identical and lacks that browser-specific restore. The native object has no source MD5 in its line table, so this file remains a weaker source association, not exact-byte provenance."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The native executable uses native host TCG; browser execution uses Emscripten TCI/Asyncify/fibers. Equal C text does not establish equal generated code, exception/stack semantics or scheduling.",
    "The present native-lock build executable has a different hash from the copied tested binary. Only the matching linked objects are used for this scoped source identification.",
    "No causal claim follows from two stable native runs. The browser warm BREAK/RESET remains an unresolved separate failure."
  ],
